\begin_layout Section
Price setting in the export markets problem: local currency assumption
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Firm 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 discriminates across countries, by invoicing and setting the price of its
 brand in the currency of the generic destination market 
\begin_inset Formula $CO$
\end_inset

.
 Hence, the local currency pricing assumption holds.
 There is sluggish price adjustment due to staggered price contracts 
\shape italic
a' la Calvo
\shape default
.
 The probability of optimally resetting prices in a given period 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 is 
\lang english

\begin_inset Formula $1−\xi_{X}$
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula $(0≤\xi_{X}≤1)$
\end_inset


\lang british
.
 All firms that receive permission to reset their price contracts in a given
 period 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 choose the same price, 
\begin_inset Formula $\widetilde{P}{}_{X,t}^{H,CO}$
\end_inset

 , while those firms which do not re-optimize update their prices according
 to the following scheme:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang english
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
P_{X,t}^{CO}(h)=\left(\Pi_{X,t-1}^{H,CO}\right)^{\chi_{X}}\overline{\Pi}^{1-\chi_{X}}P_{X,t-1}^{CO}(h)
\end{gather*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang english
and which can also be written as:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang english
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
P_{t+k}(n)=\stackrel[s=1]{k}{\prod}\left(\Pi_{NT,t+s-1}\right)^{\chi_{N}}\overline{\Pi}^{1-\chi_{N}}P_{t}(n)
\end{gather*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang english
meaning that the price contracts are indexed to a geometric average of past
 (gross) sector-specific inflation,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang english
where 
\begin_inset Formula $\Pi_{X,t-1}^{H,CO}=P{}_{X,t-1}^{H,CO}/P_{X,t-2}^{H,CO}$
\end_inset

 is the sector-specific inflation rate and the foreign inflation objective
 is assumed to be time invariant and equal to the Home long-run inflation
 objective, 
\begin_inset Formula $\overline{\Pi}^{CO}=\overline{\Pi}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

